# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import lib/bim/planar3.dl

to planar check {boolean:condition} named {string:label}:
    if condition = false:
        print line label
        @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)

to get planar v2 {a number:x} {a number:y}:
    return a cad vector2 with x x and y y

to get planar v3 {a number:x} {a number:y} {a number:z}:
    return a cad vector3 with x x, y y and z z

to planar point {cad vector3:actual} equals {cad vector3:expected}:
    planar check (((the x of actual) = (the x of expected)) and (((the y of actual) = (the y of expected)) and ((the z of actual) = (the z of expected)))) named "exact planar point"

to planar point {cad vector3:actual} is near {cad vector3:expected} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:tolerance}:
    planar check (((the absolute value of ((the x of actual) - (the x of expected))) < tolerance) and (((the absolute value of ((the y of actual) - (the y of expected))) < tolerance) and ((the absolute value of ((the z of actual) - (the z of expected))) < tolerance))) named "planar point tolerance"

to get the planar unit arc:
    return the cad curve2 of (a cad arc2 at (the cad zero vector2) with radius 1.0 from 0.0 to 1.5707963267948966)

to get the planar upright frame:
    set result to the cad orthonormal plane with origin (the cad zero vector3), x axis (the cad x axis) and normal (planar v3 0.0 -1.0 0.0)
    planar check (the valid of result) named "upright constructor"
    return the value of result

to get the planar tilted frame:
    set result to the cad orthonormal plane with origin (planar v3 3.0 4.0 5.0), x axis (planar v3 1.0 1.0 0.0) and normal (planar v3 0.0 1.0 1.0)
    planar check (the valid of result) named "tilted constructor"
    return the value of result
